# Hello, Java — jshell, jbang, Maven

## The one method that runs

```java
public static void main(String[] args) {
    System.out.println("Hello, Java");
}
```

The JVM calls **`main`** to start — memorize the shape.

## Three scales, three tools

- **`jshell`** — *experiment*: type the body, no file, no `main`

```
jshell> System.out.println("Hello, Java")
```

- **`jbang`** — *script*: run one `.java` file, `//DEPS` pulls in libraries
- **Maven** — *project*: standard layout + dependency management

```
src/main/java/App.java   ·   mvn compile · test · package
```

## The throughline

Same `main`, three scales — **try** · **script** · **build**. Climb only as far as the task needs.
